A||||5||Linx||V6 with sudden loss of power||||1||
Z||000000||Linx||01-27-2001||05:29 PM||||On a grocery ride, my '86 V6 developed a sudden loss of power.<P>It idles fine, but poppig it into gear makes it stumble and it wont cruise faster than a whoppin' ten mph.  Punchin' the gas makes it stumble and stall.<P>This is recently rebuilt and most of the sensors are new.  There arent any codes on the ecm.<P>Any ideas?||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroJoe||01-27-2001||05:47 PM||||Though I dont have a V6, I can say that it sounds like you may have a problem with your fuel pressure.  Possibly a pump or a clogged up fuel filter.  There is a schrader valve on the fuel rail, you can check the pressure there I belive.  But what pressure you should have I couldnt tell ya...<P>Im sure someone else will be able to.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Linx||01-27-2001||06:33 PM||||it aint ignition or timing...i got tons o' spark. just an amazing lack of power.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ray b||01-27-2001||07:08 PM|||| bad cat!! fix is large tool to ream out cat like tire iron, cut inlet side pipe clear to get tool in and ream it reweld or use ext. clamp to close up or replace with pipe or new cat <BR>check ext. for flow first before cutting to see if cat is pluged up no way to save it if pluged. ext. manafold will glow red if run long time     ray||||reg||1
Z||000004||88formula||01-27-2001||09:27 PM||||I agree with fierojoe. Sounds like a classic fuel pump failure or seriously clogged fuel filter.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/88formula_logo_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Elenor84||01-27-2001||11:39 PM||||Just to be safe...double  check your tps...I had a huge power loss to and It turns out that I snaped my tps wen I was doing a valve cover gasket replacement...just to be safe u know?<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank><BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Sideview.jpg">  </A>||||reg||1
